      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788081144167,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "PROBLEM \n1. We have given tasks in [number,number] => \nenqueue time : time to start processing\nprocessing time : time for processing\n\n2. Single threaded CPU means :\nat most one task at a time , cpu always \nchooses shortest processing time (Pt)\nif mutiple -> smallest index \n\n3. after starting task , it will complete the task \nwithout stopping\n\nSTRATEGY \n1. Min heap will be use to get the top priority \ntask\n\n2. I also think that a queue can be used here\nto get the upcoming tasks\n\n",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "PROBLEM \n1. We have given tasks in [number,number] => \nenqueue time : time to start processing\nprocessing time : time for processing\n\n2. Single threaded CPU means :\nat most one task at a time , cpu always \nchooses shortest processing time (Pt)\nif mutiple -> smallest index \n\n3. after starting task , it will complete the task \nwithout stopping\n\nSTRATEGY \n1. Min heap will be use to get the top priority \ntask\n\n2. I also think that a queue can be used here\nto get the upcoming tasks\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
